    "result_text": "The full test suite passes \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` is the only concrete test class (the other two files are the abstract base and a helper).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the audit-on-create requirement while keeping the audit concern in its own single-responsibility unit.\n\n**New class** \u2014 `service/OwnerAuditor.java`: a small `@Component` whose only job is emitting owner audit-trail lines. It logs via the SLF4J logger named `AUDIT`, and its `ownerCreated(Owner)` method records the owner's `id`, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate`.\n\n**Wired into** `rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`: injected `OwnerAuditor` via the constructor and called `ownerAuditor.ownerCreated(owner)` immediately after `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` in `addOwner` \u2014 the point at which the create has succeeded and the owner's id, customer code, and resolved registration date are all populated.\n\nRather than inlining a logger and message-building into the controller (which already carries substantial create-flow logic), I gave the audit logic its own class so it stays cohesive and reusable for future owner lifecycle events.\n\nThe observed output confirms the behavior:\n```\nINFO  AUDIT - Owner created: id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-09-18\n```\nand `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0 \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS`.",
